{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou","kind":"proposition","title":"Applicability of the Wenzl-bridge $y_\\lambda$ formula in QOU: Schur--Weyl + 1-dim trace space","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge"],"cites":["references/chlouveraki2016","references/wenzl1988","references/juyumaya2004"],"tags":["wenzl-bridge","applicability","schur-weyl-duality","tannaka-krein","markov-trace","uniqueness","qou-axioms"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_bridge_applicability_qou","text":"wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code> be a QOU substrate with self-dual fundamental object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> and fibre functor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau</code>. Then the Markov trace <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}_M</code> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(R, q)</code> is uniquely fixed by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> up to normalisation, and equals the Wenzl-bridge closed form.</em></p>\n<p>This ensures there is no parameter fitting. The unique Tannaka-Krein trace forces the exact Wenzl substitution at fractional rank <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.30.6"}
